sequenceDiagram
    participant Worker as Webhook Worker
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant PI as payment_intents Table
    participant Ledger as ledger_entries Table
    participant Lock as Row-Level Lock
    
    Note over Worker,Lock: Atomic Transaction: Status Update + Ledger Insert
    
    Worker->>+DB: BEGIN TRANSACTION<br/>(ISOLATION: READ COMMITTED)
    
    Worker->>+PI: UPDATE payment_intents<br/>SET status = 'succeeded'<br/>WHERE provider_tx_id = $1<br/>AND status NOT IN ('succeeded','refunded')<br/>RETURNING *
    
    Note over PI,Lock: Implicit row lock acquired<br/>Other transactions wait or skip
    
    alt Payment Found and Not Already Succeeded
        PI-->>Worker: Row returned (locked)
        
        Worker->>Worker: Compute ledger entries:<br/>- DEBIT provider: -1050<br/>- CREDIT merchant: +1020<br/>- CREDIT gateway:fees: +30
        
        Worker->>Worker: Validate SUM = 0<br/>(-1050 + 1020 + 30 = 0) ✓
        
        loop For Each Ledger Entry
            Worker->>+Ledger: INSERT INTO ledger_entries<br/>(payment_intent_id, account, amount, ...)<br/>UNIQUE(payment_intent_id, account)
            
            alt First Insert
                Ledger-->>-Worker: Success
            else Duplicate (Replay)
                Ledger-->>Worker: ERROR: duplicate key (23505)
                Worker->>DB: ROLLBACK
                DB-->>-Worker: Transaction aborted
                Note over Worker: Idempotency: ledger already exists<br/>Return success (no-op)
            end
        end
        
        Worker->>+DB: COMMIT
        
        Note over DB: ALL changes persist atomically:<br/>✓ status: processing → succeeded<br/>✓ 3 ledger rows inserted<br/>✓ updated_at timestamp
        
        DB-->>-Worker: Success
        
    else Payment Already Succeeded or Not Found
        PI-->>-Worker: No rows (RETURNING empty)
        Worker->>DB: ROLLBACK
        DB-->>-Worker: Transaction aborted
        Note over Worker: Idempotency: payment already in<br/>terminal state, no ledger write
    end
    
    Note over Worker,Lock: Failure Scenarios Protected:
    
    rect rgb(255, 240, 240)
        Note over Worker: Crash after status update but before ledger?<br/>→ ROLLBACK on connection close<br/>→ Status remains 'processing'<br/>→ Reconciler or retry will fix
    end
    
    rect rgb(255, 240, 240)
        Note over Worker: Ledger validation fails (SUM ≠ 0)?<br/>→ Application returns error<br/>→ No COMMIT issued<br/>→ Critical bug caught before persist
    end
    
    rect rgb(255, 240, 240)
        Note over Worker: Webhook delivered twice (network)?<br/>→ First: status updated + ledger created<br/>→ Second: UPDATE returns no rows (already succeeded)<br/>→ Second: ledger INSERT fails (unique constraint)<br/>→ Idempotent: both webhooks return success
    end
    
    rect rgb(240, 255, 240)
        Note over Worker: Success Guarantee:<br/>Payment status and ledger entries<br/>are committed together or not at all.<br/><br/>PostgreSQL ACID transaction<br/>ensures atomic visibility.
    end
